    "content": "On August 30, 2026, a ceremony was held in Mogadishu to mark the 104th anniversary of Turkey's Victory Day, which celebrates the decisive Battle of Dumlupınar in 1922, a turning point in Turkey's War of Independence. The event was organized by the Turkish Embassy in Mogadishu and attended by senior Somali government officials, including the Minister of Interior, Federal Affairs and Reconciliation, Ali Yusuf Ali (Xoosh), as well as diplomats and representatives from both countries.\n\nDuring the ceremony, Minister Xoosh conveyed congratulations on behalf of the Somali government and people, underscoring the significance of the day not only for Turkey but as a symbol of resilience and sovereignty. He emphasized the growing partnership between Somalia and Turkey, which has expanded in recent years across security, infrastructure, and humanitarian aid.\n\nThe anniversary serves as a reminder of Turkey's historical commitment to national independence, which resonates with Somalia's own journey toward stability. For the Somali diaspora, the event underscores the deepening ties between the two countries, which have been exemplified by Turkish investments in Mogadishu's port and airport, as well as training programs for Somali security forces.\n\nAs Somalia continues to rebuild, the alliance with Turkey represents a model of international cooperation that diaspora communities may view with optimism, fostering opportunities for economic growth and cultural exchange. The ceremony concluded with a reaffirmation of mutual respect and a shared vision for regional stability.",
